---
// Page 16 of the Beatles Bench section, written for the site.
// The command and its output come from src/data/bench/every-language.json.
// scripts/bench-replay.mjs replays the command against the pinned bench and
// fails when a byte differs.
import BenchPage from '../../layouts/BenchPage.astro';
import { SURFACES } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import run from '../../data/bench/every-language.json';

const others = SURFACES.filter((s) => s.slug !== 'shell');
const esc = (t) => t.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
const cmdHtml = run.command.split('\n').map((l, i) => `<span class="p">${i === 0 ? '$ ' : '  '}</span>${esc(l)}`).join('\n');
// A null answer is not sure. Only that mark carries colour.
const outHtml = esc(run.output.trimEnd()).replace(/("value":)(null)/g, '$1<span class="mark unsure">$2</span>');
---
<BenchPage title="One question, three answers" tagline="One question answers yes, no, or not sure.">
  <p>Every ThinkThen surface takes the same three things: a question, a text, and a bar. Here is one bench question about three songs: "It appears on the album Abbey Road." The band <code>--threshold 0.3:0.7</code> turns each probability into yes, no, or not sure.</p>

  <p>Run this in <code>examples/05-filter</code> of a bench checkout. It answers from the saved recording, with no key.</p>
  <div class="block bench-run">
    <div class="caption"><span class="grow">Replayed against the pinned bench.</span><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button></div>
    <pre class="cmd" data-copy={run.command} set:html={cmdHtml}></pre>
    <pre class="out" set:html={outHtml}></pre>
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>Octopus's Garden is on Abbey Road. At 0.75 it clears 0.7, so it reads yes.</li>
    <li>Hey Jude is not. At 0.29 it falls under 0.3, so it reads no.</li>
    <li>Penny Lane sits at 0.43, inside the band. Its answer is <code>null</code>, and a person should check it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A single bar of 0.5 would call Penny Lane no. The band admits the model is not sure.</p>

  <h2>The same question from your language</h2>
  <p>Every surface takes the same question, text, and bar. Only the command can replay a saved recording, so this page shows the command. Each language page shows how the call reads there.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    {others.map((s) => <a class="tile" href={'/' + s.slug + '/'}><b>{s.name}</b><span>How a call reads in {s.name}.</span></a>)}
  </div>
</BenchPage>
